     Making persistent changes to _/_e_t_c_/_r_e_s_o_l_v_._c_o_n_f:

           vi /etc/resolv.conf
           ...
           mount /cfg
           cp /etc/resolv.conf /cfg
           umount /cfg

     A more useful example of a customization function is the following, which
     changes the default size of the _/_e_t_c directory from 5MB to 30MB:

           cust_etc_size () (
                   cd ${NANO_WORLDDIR}/conf
                   echo 30000 > default/etc/md_size
           )
           customize_cmd cust_etc_size

